=== Direction A: Windows share mounted on Linux ===

--- 1. find the Windows host from inside WSL ---
    WSL2 is NAT'd, so the Windows host is NOT 127.0.0.1 from in here.
    Three addresses reach it, and all three were confirmed open on 445:
      172.25.112.1             445 OPEN
      host.docker.internal     445 OPEN
      192.168.65.254           445 OPEN
    using: 172.25.112.1

    NOTE: /mnt/c inside WSL is NOT this. That is a 9p/drvfs passthrough,
    not an SMB mount - no dialect, no session, no authentication. Mounting
    a Windows share properly means speaking SMB to \\host\share, which
    is what this does.

