--- 9. throughput: cold and cached, each labelled ---
    A read taken straight after a write measures the page cache, not the
    network. The first run of this script reported 9.5 GB/s over SMB -
    roughly 76x the theoretical maximum of a 1 GbE link. An impressive
    number that measured nothing. Both are reported below, labelled.

      write (to server, fsync)   : 67108864 bytes (67 MB, 64 MiB) copied, 0.788768 s, 85.1 MB/s
      read  (CACHED, not the wire): 67108864 bytes (67 MB, 64 MiB) copied, 0.00774955 s, 8.7 GB/s
      read  (COLD, over SMB)     : 67108864 bytes (67 MB, 64 MiB) copied, 2.58178 s, 26.0 MB/s
      read  (O_DIRECT, over SMB) : 67108864 bytes (67 MB, 64 MiB) copied, 2.76082 s, 24.3 MB/s

